A||N||9||FieroFanaticus2||Idle Air Control Valve replacement||||1||
Z||000000||FieroFanaticus2||07-01-2001||03:24 PM||||Does the 'WELLS' Idle Air Control Valve part number 'AC106' sold through autozone have the same pintle shape and size as the original part number?  The Original Is 10mm for the 87-88 models.  Anybody Know the autozone IAC would be a good match?||||reg||1
Z||000001||johnt671||07-01-2001||05:05 PM||||I put an Auto Zone IAC in my 84 and it has works fine.||||reg||1
Z||000002||ka4nkf||07-04-2001||12:03 AM||||This a very important valve and I would stick with AC Delco.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrgone||07-04-2001||12:07 AM||||anyone have a picture of where this valve is? i got the code too. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||mrgone||07-04-2001||03:02 PM||||bump||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroFanaticus2||07-04-2001||03:21 PM||||On my car, an '88 coupe, it is on the front of the Throttle Body.  There are two screws that hold it in place.  I can take a picture and send it to you if you'd like.  If you decide to find it for yourself and start pulling out sensors, it is the one with a metal 'cone' and a spring.  Also, one screw is easy to see and get to, the other screw is more hidden and difficult to see from a normal position.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||ka4nkf||07-04-2001||05:39 PM||||I may be wrong but the Idle control valve is located on the throtle body and I use a 30/MM socket to remove. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroFanaticus2||07-04-2001||06:03 PM||||Yeah, the older cars have a different IAC Valve than the '87 '88's do.  I'm not sure about the V6 engine though and what it has, just the 4cyl.||||reg||1
Z||000008||FieroFanaticus2||07-04-2001||06:13 PM||||This should resolve any questions.  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierofanaticus/iacinfo.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierofanaticus/iacinfo.html</A> <BR>Big Picture, be patient.<BR>[This message has been edited by FieroFanaticus2 (edited 07-04-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by FieroFanaticus2 (edited 07-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||mrgone||07-04-2001||10:24 PM||||thank you muchley. i had no idea where it was||||reg||1
